      "about": "Thirty of bgfx's examples, each a different load: 01-cubes, 05-instancing and 35-dynamic (many cubes, instances, uploads), 06-bump (textured), 33-pom (parallax occlusion mapping), 08-update and 40-svt (texture uploads, sparse virtual textures: the first run writes a 370 MB tile cache to temp/ in the workload's folder), 09-hdr, 38-bloom, 39-assao and 45-bokeh (post-processing), 10-font, 20-nanovg and 51-gpufont (text and interface), 16-shadowmaps, 19-oit and 32-particles (shadows, transparency, overdraw), 21-deferred (G-buffer and lights), 22-windows (several windows), 24-nbody and 41-tess (compute), 26-occlusion (occlusion queries), 27-terrain (terrain painting), 30-picking (GPU read-back), 31-rsm (reflective shadow maps), 37-gpudrivenrendering and 48-drawindirect (draws the GPU decides), 46-fsr (upscaling), 47-pixelformats (texture formats), 50-headless (off-screen). The 21 added after the first nine ran in native Metal and in Wine D3D12 only (not D3D11). In native Metal 26-occlusion, 37-gpudrivenrendering, 41-tess and 45-bokeh do not wait for the display (700 to 3900 FPS): compare their GPU ms with paced runs with care. Pass example to perf_record.",
